le":"Annual Report 2015","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/517334/5173340315.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2014","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/517334/5173340314.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2013","url":"https://archives.nseindia.com/annual_reports/AR_1015_MOTHERSUMI_2012_2013_16082013113942.zip","source":"the data provider"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2013","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/517334/5173340313.pdf","source":"bse"}],"analysis":{"summary":"Samvardhana Motherson International Limited reported its financial results for the second quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026, achieving record consolidated revenues of Rs 38,280 Crores for Q2 FY27 and Rs 73,524 Crores for H1 FY27. Management highlighted strong performance in the wiring harness business, supported by acquisitions, operational efficiencies, and cost optimization initiatives despite ongoing macroeconomic headwinds such as rising copper prices and geopolitical tensions. The company announced new capital expenditures and capacity expansion projects, maintaining a stable net leverage ratio while pursuing strategic inorganic growth. Samvardhana Motherson International Limited reported its highest-ever quarterly revenue in Q1 FY27, with revenue growing 17% year-on-year and EBITDA increasing by 26%. Management highlighted strong performances across core and emerging businesses, supported by right-sizing initiatives and cost optimization despite external challenges such as rising copper and polymer prices.","themes":{"guidance":[{"claim":"The company spent INR 1,614 crores on capex in the first quarter, in-line with its full year guidance of INR 6,000 crores, plus/minus 10%.","quote":"We spent INR 1,614 crores on capex in the first quarter, in-line with our full year guidance of INR 6,000 crores, plus/minus 10%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"Favourable industry momentum in the wiring harness division is expected to continue over the coming quarters.","quote":"• Favourable industry momentum expected to continue over the coming quarters","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e2713ad9-a14b-414b-8dac-a5f60346bf71.pdf"},{"claim":"Globally, the light vehicle industry de-grew by 1.8% year-on-year during the quarter, led by weaknesses in China, which de-grew by 3.1%.","quote":"Globally, the light vehicle industry de-grew by 1.8% year-on-year during the quarter, led by weaknesses in China, the largest automotive market, which de-grew by 3.1%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"South Asia, led by India, was a clear bright spot and continued to see strong growth.","quote":"South Asia, led by India, was a clear bright spot and continued to see strong growth.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"The commercial vehicle industry is estimated to have grown 5.4% year-on-year, and the outlook for the CV industry remains favorable through FY '27.","quote":"On the commercial vehicle side, a recovery in North American market has sustained the CV industry's growth momentum, which is estimated to have grown 5.4% year-on-year. The outlook for the CV industry remains favorable through FY '27.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"The company recorded a capex of Rs 1,971 Crores during the period, representing 59% of EBITDA.","quote":"Capex of Rs. 1,971 Crores (59% of EBITDA)","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e2713ad9-a14b-414b-8dac-a5f60346bf71.pdf"},{"claim":"Capex for the third consumer electronics facility is expected to be approximately INR 65 billion spread over a period of 3 years.","quote":"Capex for this third facility is expected to be approximately INR 65 billion spread over a period of 3 years, building manufacturing capacity of 40 million units annually at full scale.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"Three plants were operationalised during the quarter, and 13 facilities are at various stages of development, with 10 expected to become operational during the course of the year.","quote":"3 plants were operationalised during the quarter, and we currently have 13 facilities at various stages of development, of which 10 are expected to become operational during the course of this year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"Softening crude oil prices eased input cost pressures during the quarter, though prices have surged roughly 24% since August-end.","quote":"• Softening crude oil prices eased input cost pressures during the quarter. However, prices have surged ~24% since Aug-end","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e2713ad9-a14b-414b-8dac-a5f60346bf71.pdf"},{"claim":"EBITDA margin improved by 60 basis points year-on-year, primarily driven by restructuring initiatives in the modules and polymer business.","quote":"EBITDA grew by 26% during the quarter, ahead of revenue growth, with EBITDA margin improving by 60 basis points year-on-year. This improvement was primarily driven by the modules and polymer business, wherein the restructuring initiatives undertaken over the last 1.5 years to breathe with the market helped absorb input cost inflation and deliver year-on-year margin improvement.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"Copper prices continued to rise up 4% sequentially, creating near-term input cost pressures.","quote":"Copper prices continued to rise up 4% sequentially, following increases of 13% and 16% sequentially in the third quarter of FY '26 and the fourth quarter of FY '26, respectively. On a year-on-year basis, copper prices are now up 40%, creating near-term input cost pressures, as these costs are typically passed on to the customers with a lag of 1 or 2 quarters.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"Polymer prices in Germany were up 55% year-on-year and 66% sequentially due to geopolitically driven crude price inflation.","quote":"Geopolitically driven crude price inflation also pushed polymer prices in Germany up by 55% year-on-year and 66% sequentially.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"Management noted that crude price inflation due to geopolitical tensions in the Middle East led to higher polymers, paint, rubber, and other input costs.","quote":"Crude price inflation due to geopolitical tensions in the Middle East led to higher polymers, paint, rubber and other input costs","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=529a26ca-0108-49d8-800a-0caa7d0bcee2.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"The aerospace business order book grew by more than 17% since FY '26 end.","quote":"Our Aerospace business delivered revenue growth of over 20% year-on-year, while the order book grew by more than 17% since FY '26 end, giving us strong visibility on future growth.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"},{"claim":"The third consumer electronics facility will build manufacturing capacity of 40 million units annually at full scale.","quote":"Capex for this third facility is expected to be approximately INR 65 billion spread over a period of 3 years, building manufacturing capacity of 40 million units annually at full scale.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}],"capital_allocation":[{"claim":"The leverage ratio is at an all-time low of 0.8x, well within the financial policy ceiling of 2.5x and internal aspiration of staying below 1.5x.","quote":"Our leverage ratio is now at an all-time low of 0.8x, well within our financial policy ceiling of 2.5x and our internal aspiration of staying below 1.5x.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}],"risks_headwinds":[{"claim":"Geopolitical tensions are driving cost inflation and monetary tightness.","quote":"Geopolitical Tensions Driving Cost Inflation & Monetary Tightness.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=e2713ad9-a14b-414b-8dac-a5f60346bf71.pdf"},{"claim":"The World Container Index was up 40% year-on-year and 83% sequentially, leading to additional costs in certain instances.","quote":"Freight costs were similarly affected, with the World Container Index up 40% year-on-year and 83% sequentially. In certain instances, we incurred additional costs to ensure timely delivery to our customers.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf"}]},"management_commitments":[{"claim":"The third facility for consumer electronics remains on track for commissioning in the third quarter of FY '27.","quote":"The third facility remains on track for commissioning in the third quarter of FY '27 and will bring added upstream integration capabilities.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=4e60dd2a-3d5d-48a3-bcf6-bbdd247d505d.pdf","timeframe":"Q3 FY27"}],"coverage":{"docs_analysed":3,"kinds":["concall_ppt","concall_transcript"]}},"_meta":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash","grounded":true,"facts_kept":19,"facts_dropped_ungrounded":22,"note":"Facts are verbatim-grounded against the company's own documents; claims whose quote was not found were dropped."}}